# gdlint's config, found by walking up from the directory it is run in — so run `gdlint addons game
# tests tools` from the repo root and this applies to all of it.
#
# **What is disabled, and why: lint is only useful if a run can be read.** With the defaults the
# project produced 5 455 findings and 5 404 of them were two rules about how a file is laid out, so a
# real find — an argument nothing reads, a resource loaded twice, a line the parser chokes on — was
# invisible. These are the rules that were producing that noise:
#
#   max-line-length          5 287 findings. The long line is deliberate here: a member's doc block
#                            carries the measurement that settled a constant, and wrapping it to fit a
#                            column is how a why-comment becomes a what-comment.
#   class-definitions-order  112. It wants consts before vars; these files interleave declarations
#                            with the doc blocks that belong to them, and reordering would move a
#                            block away from the declaration it documents — the one GDScript trap that
#                            is invisible to the parser and to --check-only.
#   max-file-lines           system_scene.gd and main.gd are known-big and are being split for other
#                            reasons, not to satisfy a line count.
#   max-public-methods       same file, same reason.
#   expression-not-assigned  the two findings are `camera.global_transform` in tests/profile_costs.gd:
#                            calling it IS the measurement, and binding it to a name would let the
#                            compiler fold it.
#
# Everything else stays on. The rules that have already earned their place: unused-argument (it found
# four real ones), duplicated-load, mixed-tabs-and-spaces, trailing-whitespace, unnecessary-pass.
disable:
- max-line-length
- class-definitions-order
- max-file-lines
- max-public-methods
- expression-not-assigned
